meta {
  name: 16-Submit APPLICANT_IDENTITY verification
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/verifications
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "type": "APPLICANT_IDENTITY",
    "documentRefs": {
      "nin": {
        "url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dreamhomes-mock/image/upload/v1/temi-nin-front.jpg",
        "label": "NIN slip front"
      }
    }
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: in [201, 400, 403, 409]
}

docs {
  My persona doc says I should submit a NIN to get the verified-
  applicant badge so owners take my offers seriously. But there is
  NO file-upload endpoint for `/verifications` in the spec — only
  `documentRefs` which is a free-form `Map<String, Object>`. I
  literally have no idea what shape it expects.

  - Should the keys be specific enum values like `nin`, `passport`?
  - Should the value be a string URL or an object with a URL?
  - Where am I supposed to host the image — am I expected to
    upload to my own Cloudinary first? Where's the platform's file-
    upload?

  I'm guessing at a `{nin: {url, label}}` shape because that is the
  most "obviously correct" thing a developer would write. A real
  Lagos user filling a verification form would never figure this
  out. Major UX gap.
}
